WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.860
- With regard to General
Flynn and his unmasking,

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:06.040
I think it goes at least up to Joe Biden.

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:07.670
Joe Biden, we now have documents

00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:09.540
that were declassified yesterday

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:11.530
by Ric Grenell that show

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:14.868
that Joe Biden requested the
unmasking of General Flynn.

00:00:14.868 --> 00:00:17.451
(upbeat music)

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:25.550
- I'm Dave Rubin, and
this is The Rubin Report.

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:28.010
Quick reminder everybody
to subscribe to our channel

00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:28.900
and click that little bell so

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:31.140
so you get delivered our videos.

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:31.973
And more importantly,

00:00:31.973 --> 00:00:34.880
joining me today is the
junior senator from Kentucky

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:37.340
and the fiercest defender of liberty

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:40.080
that we have in the
United States government.

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:43.852
Senator Rand Paul, I'm thrilled
you're finally joining us.

00:00:43.852 --> 00:00:46.690
- I'm glad to Dave,
glad to be on your show.

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:48.330
- All right, so let's dive in.

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:49.910
I think we're just gonna
split this interview,

00:00:49.910 --> 00:00:51.160
I know you've got about a half hour.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:53.000
We're gonna just split it into two parts.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:55.060
Let's spend the first half talking about

00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:59.340
this FISA Amendment
that you just proposed.

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:01.730
Can you just talk a little
bit about why you did it,

00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:03.140
what's going on with surveillance?

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:06.000
I sense people are seriously confused

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.360
about the whole Flynn case,

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:10.500
what the Obama administration
may or may not have known.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:12.300
So if you could just kinda do a 101

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:15.330
to clean up some of that,
that would be great.

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:16.400
- Well the FISA Court is the

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:18.410
Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Court,

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:21.490
and it was set up in the '70s basically to

00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:24.590
investigate, spy on, surveil

00:01:24.590 --> 00:01:27.650
foreigners and possible terrorists.

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:29.330
It was never intended for it to be used

00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:31.360
against political candidates,

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:34.480
or to investigate American
political campaigns

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:36.180
or American political figures.

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:37.200
But as everybody knows,

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:40.220
this is what the secret
court that they used

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:43.200
to go after President Trump in 2016

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:45.080
in the summer and the fall.

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:46.060
And,

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:49.210
I think this was a horrendous
abuse of power and,

00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:51.920
using a secret court
to go after an American

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:54.420
I think is a travesty of justice.

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:58.620
So this is a court that lacks
constitutional protections.

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:00.310
When you go to a regular court,

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:02.190
a constitutional court
that was established

00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:04.530
by Article III of the Constitution,

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:05.500
you get a lawyer,

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:07.300
that's one obvious thing you get.

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:08.860
But you also get the Fourth Amendment.

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:11.040
The Fourth Amendment says that

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:12.320
they can't search your house,

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:14.070
or your phone, or any of these things

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:15.660
unless they go to a judge

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:17.810
and they have to say that
there's probable cause

00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:19.065
that you committed a crime.

00:02:19.065 --> 00:02:20.830
It's a fairly high standard,

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:23.040
but it's the constitutional standard.

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:25.980
In the FISA Court, they
go do it and they say,

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:27.620
well, you just have to have probable calls

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:30.890
that we think you are associated
with a foreign government.

00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:32.230
So that's what they did with Carter Page.

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:34.630
They said, "Oh, we see
you talk to the Russians."

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:35.463
And he said,

00:02:35.463 --> 00:02:37.447
"Well, yeah I told the CIA.

00:02:37.447 --> 00:02:39.187
"I've run into Russians, I do business,

00:02:39.187 --> 00:02:40.607
"I'm in these think tanks.

00:02:40.607 --> 00:02:42.267
"And I told the CIA,

00:02:42.267 --> 00:02:44.157
"and they know that I've
talked to the Russians before

00:02:44.157 --> 00:02:46.400
"and I've tried to give them information."

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:48.840
They discounted all of
that, lied to the FISA Court

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:51.870
and then, what began this
whole Trump investigation.

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:53.280
But here's my point.

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:55.310
A lot of Republicans,
a lot of conservatives,

00:02:55.310 --> 00:02:56.880
lot of Libertarians who are upset.

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:58.400
How do you fix it?

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:02.400
One way of doing it is to try
to make the FISA Court system

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.560
more like a constitutional court.

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:07.800
So add protections, in
the scheme of things.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:08.930
But here's my point.

00:03:08.930 --> 00:03:11.800
I don't think it's possible
to make it constitutional.

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:14.590
They don't notify you that
they're investigating you,

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:16.150
so it's secret.

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:17.810
You don't get a lawyer.

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:20.810
Some of the reforms are to
give you a friend, an amicus,

00:03:20.810 --> 00:03:22.320
so somebody a friend of the court,

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:24.040
that argues for you but
they still don't tell you

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:25.140
you've been accused of anything,

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:29.450
so you don't really direct a
lawyer to direct your defense.

00:03:29.450 --> 00:03:31.700
And so, I don't think it fixes the system.

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:34.610
So my amendment would simply say this,

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:37.350
the FISA Court really isn't
constitutional for Americans

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:39.620
so let's exempt Americans from it,

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:41.110
and let's use it only on foreigners.

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:42.780
It is, for all,

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:45.010
it's called the Foreign
Intelligence Court.

00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:47.060
Why don't we go after foreigners with it?

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:48.010
And people say, well,

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:51.610
what if there really was a
spy in a political campaign?

00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:52.880
What would you do?

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:55.440
Well, use the Constitution, go to a judge,

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:58.040
ask for a warrant to search the person

00:03:58.040 --> 00:03:59.630
or to surveil the person.

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:01.680
And judges do grant things like that,

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:02.850
but you have to evidence.

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:04.760
But you'd also have to
obey the Bill of Rights

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:05.990
and the Fourth Amendment.

00:04:05.990 --> 00:04:07.720
That's what I'm for but unfortunately,

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:08.790
I'm in the minority up here.

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:10.861
I think that would win
with your crowd watching,

00:04:10.861 --> 00:04:13.660
(Dave laughs)
but I'm afraid it probably,

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:16.270
it didn't have enough
votes in the Senate to win.

00:04:16.270 --> 00:04:18.597
- Yeah, well I assure you
you're doing just fine

00:04:18.597 --> 00:04:21.140
and the majority on my audience and

00:04:21.140 --> 00:04:22.400
we've got some work to do there.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:24.300
So can you just clarify a little bit?

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:26.810
It seemed that sort of
right leaning Twitter,

00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:28.750
let's call it right now is saying,

00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:31.710
that this stuff really went
up the chain of command,

00:04:31.710 --> 00:04:35.370
and it's possible now that
Biden and/or Obama themselves

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:36.980
actually knew about it

00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:39.080
and we're instigating some of this stuff.

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:42.053
What's the actual evidence at this point?

00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:47.320
- Well, with regard to General
Flynn and his unmasking,

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:49.490
I think it goes at least up to Joe Biden.

00:04:49.490 --> 00:04:51.100
Joe Biden, we now have documents

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:52.980
that were declassified yesterday

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:54.980
by Ric Grenell that show

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:58.010
that Joe Biden requested the
unmasking of General Flynn.

00:04:58.010 --> 00:04:59.770
What does that mean?

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:03.110
They get like a national
security or a FISA warrant

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:07.360
to listen to the phone call
of the Russian ambassador.

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:08.730
I can kind of understand that.

00:05:08.730 --> 00:05:10.580
We spy on ambassadors, they spy on us.

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:12.420
That goes on all around the world.

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:15.290
But if that ambassador is talking to a

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:16.960
person who's elected to our government,

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:19.550
or part of the administration
like General Flynn,

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:20.383
they're supposed to say,

00:05:20.383 --> 00:05:21.620
oh, no he's talking to an American,

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:23.050
we're not supposed to listen.

00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:24.170
Or if we listen,

00:05:24.170 --> 00:05:27.210
we're not supposed to unmask that person.

00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:28.990
Well, the thing is if
you're a prominent person,

00:05:28.990 --> 00:05:30.530
a lot of people know you by your voice

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:32.960
and you may well introduce
yourself by saying,

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:35.930
Mr. Ambassador this is General Flynn.

00:05:35.930 --> 00:05:37.460
So it's kind of,
- [Dave] Sure.

00:05:37.460 --> 00:05:39.800
- it's hard to really completely mask it.

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:41.120
But here's the point.

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:43.110
You're only supposed to unmask that person

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:44.710
if there's national security reasons.

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:46.970
So if they're plotting to attack the U.S,

00:05:46.970 --> 00:05:48.310
you'd say well, that's reasonable.

00:05:48.310 --> 00:05:50.550
You'd unmask them and
try to stop the plot.

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:52.290
But if they're discussing policy,

00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:54.860
and the person is the
National Security Advisor,

00:05:54.860 --> 00:05:57.620
there would be absolutely no reason,

00:05:57.620 --> 00:05:59.840
other than a politically motivated one.

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:01.920
So if this is politically motivated,

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:05.350
then it becomes illegal
surveillance, illegal eavesdropping.

00:06:05.350 --> 00:06:07.980
And really, you remember we
had this impeachment trial

00:06:07.980 --> 00:06:10.070
over them saying someone in government

00:06:10.070 --> 00:06:12.860
used government to go
after a political opponent.

00:06:12.860 --> 00:06:15.860
Turns out, what they did to General Flynn

00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:17.322
sounds exactly like that they abused

00:06:17.322 --> 00:06:18.820
- [Dave] Yeah.
- government,

00:06:18.820 --> 00:06:22.580
they used surveillance to go
after their political opponent.

00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:25.870
- Are you worried, for
a limited government guy

00:06:25.870 --> 00:06:28.810
you don't want the administrative
state to be too big,

00:06:28.810 --> 00:06:31.930
it's like you can get in the
weeds on all of this stuff

00:06:31.930 --> 00:06:32.763
but in many ways,

00:06:32.763 --> 00:06:34.820
this is what you've spent
your whole life fighting,

00:06:34.820 --> 00:06:37.810
that the whole system
has just gotten so big

00:06:37.810 --> 00:06:39.490
and crazy at this point,

00:06:39.490 --> 00:06:42.330
that even if you tell people what's true,

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:43.760
and we have all the facts in front of us

00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:45.930
that sort of, the ship has sailed

00:06:45.930 --> 00:06:48.290
on reining in the things
that I think you and I

00:06:48.290 --> 00:06:50.790
and most of my audience are worried about.

00:06:50.790 --> 00:06:52.510
- Yes and no.

00:06:52.510 --> 00:06:54.510
I think if you would ask
your audience, obviously,

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:57.220
it's probably a very
limited government audience.

00:06:57.220 --> 00:06:59.380
But even if you ask a general audience.

00:06:59.380 --> 00:07:02.520
So for example, if I ask
everybody in Kentucky

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:04.840
about whether or not a secret court

00:07:04.840 --> 00:07:05.960
where you don't get a lawyer

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:08.090
should investigate political campaigns,

00:07:08.090 --> 00:07:10.220
I would say oppose it 75%,

00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:11.850
particularly if you keep Trump out of it.

00:07:11.850 --> 00:07:13.290
Now Trump's pretty popular in my state

00:07:13.290 --> 00:07:14.650
so it doesn't hurt so much,

00:07:14.650 --> 00:07:16.530
but really if you could
get Trump out of it.

00:07:16.530 --> 00:07:18.110
But the problem is,

00:07:18.110 --> 00:07:21.160
people get that they won't
vote on principle and ideas so

00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:22.203
I didn't get any Democratic votes on this.

00:07:22.203 --> 00:07:25.670
I only got 11 Republicans,
but I got no Democrats.

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:28.520
Even though many of them profess to

00:07:28.520 --> 00:07:30.470
think that FISA has too much power

00:07:30.470 --> 00:07:31.940
and shouldn't be investigating Americans,

00:07:31.940 --> 00:07:34.530
they wouldn't vote for it
cause they saw it as a vote

00:07:34.530 --> 00:07:36.350
rebuking FISA over Trump.

00:07:36.350 --> 00:07:39.110
And so they saw it as a political vote.

00:07:39.110 --> 00:07:40.610
But I guess I don't look at it this way.

00:07:40.610 --> 00:07:41.763
I lose a lot of times.

00:07:43.467 --> 00:07:45.706
I'm used to losing on votes in the Senate.

00:07:45.706 --> 00:07:46.539
(Dave laughs)

00:07:46.539 --> 00:07:47.372
But I think most of this,

00:07:47.372 --> 00:07:50.660
and this is where we do have some ability

00:07:50.660 --> 00:07:54.970
so we pass out a sheet of prominent tweets

00:07:54.970 --> 00:07:56.130
that went out from senators

00:07:56.130 --> 00:07:57.970
each week on Wednesday.

00:07:57.970 --> 00:08:00.140
And our office does this sheet.

00:08:00.140 --> 00:08:02.557
And they all complain because
we'll put out something

00:08:02.557 --> 00:08:05.494
and my tweet will have
gotten 30,000 retweets

00:08:05.494 --> 00:08:07.190
and then we'll put out Senator so-and-so,

00:08:07.190 --> 00:08:08.784
and they got six.

00:08:08.784 --> 00:08:09.740
(Dave laughs)
- So, right,

00:08:09.740 --> 00:08:12.180
one of the things they see is that

00:08:12.180 --> 00:08:16.070
the Liberty Movement has
reached well beyond them

00:08:16.070 --> 00:08:17.470
and they fear the election.

00:08:17.470 --> 00:08:18.930
These people are afraid of elections,

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:19.763
they're afraid of me,

00:08:19.763 --> 00:08:21.120
they're afraid of conservatives

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:23.100
cause they're afraid someday
someone's gonna wake up

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:24.580
and challenge them in the primary.

00:08:24.580 --> 00:08:26.570
And that's what has to happen.

00:08:26.570 --> 00:08:28.660
The Democrats, it's sort of like this.

00:08:28.660 --> 00:08:30.460
Democrats don't care at
all about the deficit

00:08:30.460 --> 00:08:31.293
and they'll tell you.

00:08:31.293 --> 00:08:33.160
They wanna spend more money,
they're honest about it.

00:08:33.160 --> 00:08:35.090
Republicans,

00:08:35.090 --> 00:08:36.590
well, say they're against debt,

00:08:36.590 --> 00:08:38.750
say they're against
spending but they're also,

00:08:38.750 --> 00:08:41.020
most of them, big government Republicans,

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:42.640
vote lockstep with the Democrats.

00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:45.350
So really, when people
ask me whose fault is it,

00:08:45.350 --> 00:08:46.490
Republican or Democrat?

00:08:46.490 --> 00:08:50.890
I say yeah, it is really
both party's fault.

00:08:50.890 --> 00:08:53.200
But, we could give up,

00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:54.710
and just try to protect ourselves,

00:08:54.710 --> 00:08:57.167
but, I think if we give up

00:08:57.167 --> 00:08:59.930
and the few good voices here go away,

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:03.380
then really I think it goes
much quicker toward Socialism,

00:09:03.380 --> 00:09:06.280
it goes much quicker towards
indebtedness and big government

00:09:06.280 --> 00:09:08.520
so there has to be some voices.

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:09.900
There needs to be more.

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:12.803
The newer people up here I
think are frankly better than,

00:09:13.670 --> 00:09:15.180
the ones that have been here a long time.

00:09:15.180 --> 00:09:20.180
So I have good conversations
with Senator Braun,

00:09:20.180 --> 00:09:21.890
Senator Rick Scott from Florida,

00:09:21.890 --> 00:09:25.740
and who I think are open to (mumbles)

00:09:27.463 --> 00:09:29.510
to vote with me on my FISA Amendment.

00:09:29.510 --> 00:09:33.850
Mike Lee, who is with me
on the FISA Amendment also.

00:09:33.850 --> 00:09:35.270
- Can you talk a little bit about

00:09:35.270 --> 00:09:37.010
your relationship with Trump?

00:09:37.010 --> 00:09:38.350
Because one of the things that I've said

00:09:38.350 --> 00:09:40.190
to my audience repeatedly is,

00:09:40.190 --> 00:09:41.980
first off I should tell
you you'll appreciate this,

00:09:41.980 --> 00:09:43.320
I voted for Gary Johnson.

00:09:43.320 --> 00:09:46.230
I'm here in California
and I had the luxury of,

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:47.730
doing a third-party situation

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:50.140
which obviously certain people,
depending on where you live,

00:09:50.140 --> 00:09:52.700
you didn't have the luxury of doing that.

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:54.550
But I wanted to make a vote for liberty

00:09:54.550 --> 00:09:55.420
more than anything else.

00:09:55.420 --> 00:09:57.240
But one of the reasons that I've become

00:09:57.240 --> 00:10:00.590
more okay with Trump over
the last couple of years

00:10:00.590 --> 00:10:03.760
is that the guy that I
respect most in the Senate,

00:10:03.760 --> 00:10:06.430
you, has become one of his big allies.

00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:08.820
And my feeling was well, if Rand Paul,

00:10:08.820 --> 00:10:11.410
who I aligned with on so
much of the liberty stuff,

00:10:11.410 --> 00:10:14.090
sees something in him
that he can work with,

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:16.310
then I view that as a net good.

00:10:16.310 --> 00:10:17.780
Can you talk about, a little bit about

00:10:17.780 --> 00:10:19.930
your relationship
personally, but also just

00:10:19.930 --> 00:10:22.370
what do you think his actual
governing principles are?

00:10:22.370 --> 00:10:24.680
Cause it's hard to say they're
traditionally conservative

00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:27.480
or Republican or whatever else.

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:32.230
- He doesn't come from a
steeped, developed nation

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:35.070
of possibly, of Libertarianism.

00:10:35.070 --> 00:10:38.040
However, when you talk to him about war

00:10:38.040 --> 00:10:39.830
and he talks about the Iraq War,

00:10:39.830 --> 00:10:42.080
he gets it more than any other Republican,

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:45.230
obviously other than my
dad or myself or Mike Lee.

00:10:45.230 --> 00:10:47.640
He get it, and he says the
Iraq War was a mistake.

00:10:47.640 --> 00:10:49.650
He was unafraid to criticize the Bush's

00:10:49.650 --> 00:10:51.860
for making what he said was the biggest

00:10:51.860 --> 00:10:54.350
foreign policy blunder
of the last few decades.

00:10:54.350 --> 00:10:55.800
And he's right about that.

00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:57.740
And if you talk to him
he'll tell you consistently,

00:10:57.740 --> 00:10:59.610
he wants to bring the troops
home from Afghanistan,

00:10:59.610 --> 00:11:01.110
he wants to end the war.

00:11:01.110 --> 00:11:03.560
But here's the problem
is it is a tug of war.

00:11:03.560 --> 00:11:05.840
I tried to influence and,

00:11:05.840 --> 00:11:07.420
really I don't think
you can change people,

00:11:07.420 --> 00:11:09.680
I think you can tug at their instincts

00:11:09.680 --> 00:11:11.470
and try to bring them in a direction

00:11:11.470 --> 00:11:13.230
they may already believe in,

00:11:13.230 --> 00:11:15.680
and I think he already
does believe those things.

00:11:15.680 --> 00:11:17.970
The hard part is he's
been surrounded often,

00:11:17.970 --> 00:11:20.330
and many of his appointees
have been people

00:11:20.330 --> 00:11:22.360
with opposite opinion of ours,

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:24.100
but also opposite opinion
of the presidents.

00:11:24.100 --> 00:11:26.100
John Bolton was a disaster.

00:11:26.100 --> 00:11:30.180
John Bolton sort of is the
antithesis of Libertarianism.

00:11:30.180 --> 00:11:32.350
He's a big spending hawk

00:11:32.350 --> 00:11:34.170
and never met a war he didn't like.

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:37.260
And never met a civil
liberty he wouldn't trample.

00:11:37.260 --> 00:11:39.430
And yet, he got picked
and was on the inside,

00:11:39.430 --> 00:11:40.460
but he was there everyday,

00:11:40.460 --> 00:11:42.530
and I'm talking to the
President once a week,

00:11:42.530 --> 00:11:44.070
so imagine disadvantage.

00:11:44.070 --> 00:11:46.130
Lindsey Graham's on
that same side as well,

00:11:46.130 --> 00:11:48.070
so we, he's pushing one way,

00:11:48.070 --> 00:11:49.360
we're pushing the other.

00:11:49.360 --> 00:11:50.660
But I can tell you in private,

00:11:50.660 --> 00:11:52.930
when it's the President,
I, and Lindsey Graham,

00:11:52.930 --> 00:11:55.610
he'll often rebuke if
not always rebuke Graham

00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:59.070
for being for so much war,
being for perpetual war.

00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:01.010
All that being said,

00:12:01.010 --> 00:12:03.370
Libertarians, limited government people,

00:12:03.370 --> 00:12:05.660
people who want less war
who are conservatives,

00:12:05.660 --> 00:12:06.580
all get frustrated.

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:08.200
It's like, well how can we have about

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:09.060
the same amount of troops?

00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:11.260
We got more troops in Saudi Arabia.

00:12:11.260 --> 00:12:12.850
But also look at it this way.

00:12:12.850 --> 00:12:15.410
It's always a balance of
how, of what it could be.

00:12:15.410 --> 00:12:16.340
So for example,

00:12:16.340 --> 00:12:18.140
the conflict with Iran,

00:12:18.140 --> 00:12:20.440
had you had Lindsey Graham
as president during that,

00:12:20.440 --> 00:12:22.240
we would have blown up Iran.

00:12:22.240 --> 00:12:23.920
We would've had a whole war.

00:12:23.920 --> 00:12:25.820
We may well of had regime
change and people say,

00:12:25.820 --> 00:12:26.740
oh that'd be good.

00:12:26.740 --> 00:12:28.210
Well, but it could be chaos,

00:12:28.210 --> 00:12:31.120
and it could be another
10 or 15 years of chaos

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:31.953
in that region.

00:12:31.953 --> 00:12:32.786
So,

00:12:32.786 --> 00:12:34.650
I think the President does show restrain.

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:36.340
They shot a drone down.

00:12:36.340 --> 00:12:37.410
Of course they said they didn't,

00:12:37.410 --> 00:12:38.815
but I mean, all evidence pointed

00:12:38.815 --> 00:12:39.648
(Dave laughs)
towards them shooting

00:12:39.648 --> 00:12:40.481
a drone down.

00:12:40.481 --> 00:12:42.020
And the President showed restraint.

00:12:42.020 --> 00:12:43.717
He said, "Well nobody was killed

00:12:43.717 --> 00:12:46.417
"and they were encouraging me,

00:12:46.417 --> 00:12:47.837
"everybody wanted me to attack Iran.

00:12:47.837 --> 00:12:49.817
"It was gonna be limited
but we're gonna kill,

00:12:49.817 --> 00:12:52.520
"I don't know, 150 or 450 or something."

00:12:52.520 --> 00:12:54.207
He just said,

00:12:54.207 --> 00:12:55.467
"We're just not gonna do it."

00:12:55.467 --> 00:12:57.730
And I think there's a great,

00:12:57.730 --> 00:13:00.720
there's statesmanship in restraint and

00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:02.130
I think he shows that.

00:13:02.130 --> 00:13:03.830
I think his instincts are good on war

00:13:03.830 --> 00:13:06.630
and I think Libertarians who decide,

00:13:06.630 --> 00:13:08.810
I wanna affect the election,

00:13:08.810 --> 00:13:10.770
not mine as a battleground state.

00:13:10.770 --> 00:13:13.580
I think we should look
for things like that.

00:13:13.580 --> 00:13:15.660
Is he a perfect Libertarian?

00:13:15.660 --> 00:13:17.700
No, he doesn't seem to be
too concerned with debt

00:13:17.700 --> 00:13:19.470
or really decides in
the scope of government

00:13:19.470 --> 00:13:21.370
as much as many of us would wish,

00:13:21.370 --> 00:13:24.330
but on war he has some
instincts towards less war,

00:13:24.330 --> 00:13:25.780
less intervention,

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:29.330
on money we spend overseas
and international agencies

00:13:29.330 --> 00:13:31.710
and all this stuff that we
give up our sovereignty,

00:13:31.710 --> 00:13:34.700
And these international agencies, blast us

00:13:36.153 --> 00:13:38.310
and harangue us and
tell us how evil we are

00:13:38.310 --> 00:13:39.550
while cashing our checks

00:13:39.550 --> 00:13:41.820
that pays for all of their salaries.

00:13:41.820 --> 00:13:44.130
He's very good on understanding that

00:13:44.130 --> 00:13:47.460
and thinking that other people
need to pay their fair share.

00:13:47.460 --> 00:13:50.323
And so, there's a lot to be
said that's good and then,

00:13:51.490 --> 00:13:53.500
it is always, we're all,

00:13:53.500 --> 00:13:55.350
I tell people, if you want
the perfect candidate,

00:13:55.350 --> 00:13:57.085
run for office yourself.

00:13:57.085 --> 00:13:57.918
(Dave laughs)

00:13:57.918 --> 00:13:58.970
Otherwise you're always picking

00:13:58.970 --> 00:14:00.760
and choosing and trying to find the best

00:14:00.760 --> 00:14:02.965
that you can possibly find.
- Yeah.

00:14:02.965 --> 00:14:03.798
So, all right.

00:14:03.798 --> 00:14:06.160
Let's shift a little bit
towards corona and stimulus

00:14:06.160 --> 00:14:07.440
and just what's happening broadly.

00:14:07.440 --> 00:14:09.920
I'm finding right now
that there actually is

00:14:09.920 --> 00:14:13.360
a really nice moment for
liberty-minded people

00:14:13.360 --> 00:14:15.880
because one of the things that
we're suddenly talking about

00:14:15.880 --> 00:14:18.180
in America that we never talk about or,

00:14:18.180 --> 00:14:20.240
when I go to Libertarian
conferences they talk about it

00:14:20.240 --> 00:14:21.570
but nobody else talks about it,

00:14:21.570 --> 00:14:23.010
is states' rights.

00:14:23.010 --> 00:14:25.400
That is actually something being discussed

00:14:25.400 --> 00:14:26.650
at a national level right now.

00:14:26.650 --> 00:14:27.940
I think people are realizing

00:14:27.940 --> 00:14:29.830
they should be able to
protect their family,

00:14:29.830 --> 00:14:31.400
so talking about the Second Amendment.

00:14:31.400 --> 00:14:33.150
I think people are realizing that

00:14:33.150 --> 00:14:35.400
maybe they don't wanna be
in giant cities anymore,

00:14:35.400 --> 00:14:36.810
and I sense we're gonna have some really

00:14:36.810 --> 00:14:39.380
interesting population things changing.

00:14:39.380 --> 00:14:42.360
Do you sense that because of coronavirus,

00:14:42.360 --> 00:14:45.807
that the Liberty Movement
and people realizing that

00:14:45.807 --> 00:14:47.940
your congressman and your senator

00:14:47.940 --> 00:14:49.900
are way more important,

00:14:49.900 --> 00:14:51.250
or should be way more important

00:14:51.250 --> 00:14:53.490
to your life than your President,

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:55.410
are you hoping that
something might crack here?

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:57.170
I mean, I'm even seeing lefties say

00:14:57.170 --> 00:14:59.560
we should lower taxes
on people now because

00:14:59.560 --> 00:15:01.410
they need more money in their pocket.

00:15:02.310 --> 00:15:04.790
- Well, you're optimistic and I'm glad

00:15:04.790 --> 00:15:06.810
you're optimistic on it.

00:15:06.810 --> 00:15:08.150
I would say this.

00:15:08.150 --> 00:15:11.940
I would say one of the lessons
we can and should learn from

00:15:11.940 --> 00:15:15.070
the way government responds to this virus,

00:15:15.070 --> 00:15:17.000
is that one size doesn't fit all.

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:18.780
And that would go along with federalism.

00:15:18.780 --> 00:15:20.680
And that would go along with really,

00:15:20.680 --> 00:15:23.930
you should try to devolve to
the smallest governmental unit

00:15:23.930 --> 00:15:25.220
and really be on that.

00:15:25.220 --> 00:15:26.570
The Ninth Amendment says,

00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:28.920
the rights not listed
are not to be disparaged

00:15:28.920 --> 00:15:31.700
but they're to be left to
the states and the people.

00:15:31.700 --> 00:15:33.940
It's important it's not
just state governments cause

00:15:33.940 --> 00:15:36.557
state governments can
be tyrannical as well.

00:15:36.557 --> 00:15:38.750
But really, and the people.

00:15:38.750 --> 00:15:42.160
The problem we have is even
though we have devolved,

00:15:42.160 --> 00:15:44.340
most of Trump's pronouncements,

00:15:44.340 --> 00:15:46.150
even the ones that have been restrictive,

00:15:46.150 --> 00:15:48.560
have been guidelines without penalties.

00:15:48.560 --> 00:15:50.710
Most of the penalties, and
most of the punishment,

00:15:50.710 --> 00:15:52.480
most of the absolute
shutdown of the economy,

00:15:52.480 --> 00:15:53.630
came from governors.

00:15:53.630 --> 00:15:55.310
So even though it did devolve the states,

00:15:55.310 --> 00:15:58.020
the states were, and my state included.

00:15:58.020 --> 00:16:00.160
My governor is a just,

00:16:00.160 --> 00:16:02.030
I call him DWP.

00:16:02.030 --> 00:16:03.660
Drunk with power.

00:16:03.660 --> 00:16:06.200
The guys intoxicated with his own power.

00:16:06.200 --> 00:16:07.170
But here's what happened.

00:16:07.170 --> 00:16:09.100
In our state, the legislature,

00:16:09.100 --> 00:16:10.420
who knows when, years ago,

00:16:10.420 --> 00:16:12.290
passed an emergency action bill

00:16:12.290 --> 00:16:14.830
and said the governor gets
it during an emergency.

00:16:14.830 --> 00:16:17.523
And I think he even gets
to declare the emergency.

00:16:17.523 --> 00:16:19.270
I mean, there's no check and balance.

00:16:19.270 --> 00:16:22.150
Our legislator can't call
themselves back in session.

00:16:22.150 --> 00:16:24.190
We have a majority Republican legislature.

00:16:24.190 --> 00:16:25.560
They have no say.

00:16:25.560 --> 00:16:28.533
The governor has become
essentially the sole,

00:16:29.470 --> 00:16:31.840
and unique, and all powerful person

00:16:31.840 --> 00:16:33.510
that dictates everything
about the economy.

00:16:33.510 --> 00:16:35.060
He closed everything down,

00:16:35.060 --> 00:16:36.530
and he's still saying things like,

00:16:36.530 --> 00:16:39.750
well, we're not gonna
have child care open up

00:16:39.750 --> 00:16:41.290
until we get a vaccine.

00:16:41.290 --> 00:16:42.210
It's like, really?

00:16:42.210 --> 00:16:43.710
So working parents aren't going back,

00:16:43.710 --> 00:16:45.650
what if we never get a vaccine?

00:16:45.650 --> 00:16:48.750
He banned church, he
banned interstate travel.

00:16:48.750 --> 00:16:51.170
The court struck him down on both of those

00:16:51.170 --> 00:16:53.990
but he keeps on going and he acts as if

00:16:53.990 --> 00:16:57.360
he's really out there to
try to help save the people.

00:16:57.360 --> 00:16:59.250
We've had a little bit over 300 deaths,

00:16:59.250 --> 00:17:01.670
and that's sad if it was
somebody in your family,

00:17:01.670 --> 00:17:04.470
but that really, the number
of deaths in Kentucky

00:17:04.470 --> 00:17:06.700
closely mirror the flu from before.

00:17:06.700 --> 00:17:08.910
I'm not saying this is
the traditional flu,

00:17:08.910 --> 00:17:11.040
but I am saying in certain states,

00:17:11.040 --> 00:17:13.860
the outcome has not
been worse than the flu.

00:17:13.860 --> 00:17:15.690
The other thing about one-size-fit-all

00:17:15.690 --> 00:17:17.313
that we need to recognize is,

00:17:18.540 --> 00:17:21.820
young people have almost
a zero mortality to this.

00:17:21.820 --> 00:17:24.540
Zero to 18, almost zero.

00:17:24.540 --> 00:17:26.630
Less than the flu, they
don't wanna hear it.

00:17:26.630 --> 00:17:29.990
But zero to 18 deaths among
children is less than the flu.

00:17:29.990 --> 00:17:31.310
Flue is more deadly.

00:17:31.310 --> 00:17:33.050
Now if it goes up, it's the opposite.

00:17:33.050 --> 00:17:34.860
When you get to 70 and 80,

00:17:34.860 --> 00:17:36.340
particularly if you're 80 and above

00:17:36.340 --> 00:17:37.700
and you are in a nursing home,

00:17:37.700 --> 00:17:39.930
it might be 20 or 25% mortality

00:17:39.930 --> 00:17:43.040
which is 50 times worse than the flu.

00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:45.560
So, but that means maybe we
should have a different strategy

00:17:45.560 --> 00:17:48.100
for the kids than we have for the elderly.

00:17:48.100 --> 00:17:50.320
And maybe we didn't have
to close the economy down.

00:17:50.320 --> 00:17:52.210
Maybe we could've done what Sweden did

00:17:52.210 --> 00:17:54.130
and not close the schools down.

00:17:54.130 --> 00:17:56.700
We still have knuckleheads
like my governor

00:17:56.700 --> 00:17:59.020
who wanted to keep schools
closed in the fall.

00:17:59.020 --> 00:18:01.720
It's a disaster, the
economy can't function.

00:18:01.720 --> 00:18:04.010
Many people work with
their kids in school,

00:18:04.010 --> 00:18:05.900
that's where their kids go,

00:18:05.900 --> 00:18:08.680
it's a form of a place for your kids to go

00:18:08.680 --> 00:18:10.060
while the parents work.

00:18:10.060 --> 00:18:12.520
And so we've gotta open the schools but,

00:18:12.520 --> 00:18:14.030
that's the biggest thing we have to do

00:18:14.030 --> 00:18:14.863
and you're right,

00:18:14.863 --> 00:18:17.337
some of it devolves back to
states and we should want more.

00:18:17.337 --> 00:18:19.040
But really we shouldn't stop

00:18:19.040 --> 00:18:21.070
the devolution of power with the governor,

00:18:21.070 --> 00:18:22.720
we gotta go to the cities mayors,

00:18:22.720 --> 00:18:24.040
and really ultimately,

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:27.030
if you own your business,
it's your business and,

00:18:27.030 --> 00:18:29.780
you're gonna have to
respond to public pressure.

00:18:29.780 --> 00:18:31.540
I don't have to tell you what to do.

00:18:31.540 --> 00:18:32.867
But if you own a restaurant and you say

00:18:32.867 --> 00:18:34.300
I'm gonna do nothing,

00:18:34.300 --> 00:18:35.570
you're gonna get some people like me

00:18:35.570 --> 00:18:36.403
who have already had it,

00:18:36.403 --> 00:18:37.970
would love to come to your restaurant.

00:18:37.970 --> 00:18:39.780
But a lot of people are gonna be worried

00:18:39.780 --> 00:18:40.960
you're gonna have to do other things.

00:18:40.960 --> 00:18:43.230
You may have to have a
senior citizens section,

00:18:43.230 --> 00:18:44.960
you may have to have some spacing.

00:18:44.960 --> 00:18:46.400
But if the government mandates it,

00:18:46.400 --> 00:18:47.330
they'll be idiots.

00:18:47.330 --> 00:18:48.997
They'll tell everybody
to sit six feet apart,

00:18:48.997 --> 00:18:50.720
and if I've got five kids,

00:18:50.720 --> 00:18:52.850
I don't need to socially
distance from my kids.

00:18:52.850 --> 00:18:55.830
We should all sit at one
table on top of each other.

00:18:55.830 --> 00:18:56.663
You know?

00:18:56.663 --> 00:18:58.150
But if the government mandates it,

00:18:58.150 --> 00:19:00.220
they're gonna do ridiculous things.

00:19:00.220 --> 00:19:02.090
Businesses will figure this out.

00:19:02.090 --> 00:19:04.380
Churches will figure this out.

00:19:04.380 --> 00:19:06.150
If your mother's 85 years old

00:19:06.150 --> 00:19:07.500
and she lives in a small town

00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:09.400
and 20 people go to her church,

00:19:09.400 --> 00:19:12.020
and they'll space out in the church

00:19:12.020 --> 00:19:13.030
and she wants to go,

00:19:13.030 --> 00:19:14.520
by golly let her go.

00:19:14.520 --> 00:19:16.230
But if your mother's 85 years old

00:19:16.230 --> 00:19:18.280
and she goes to a mega
church with 2,000 people

00:19:18.280 --> 00:19:19.890
crammed into the pews,

00:19:19.890 --> 00:19:21.400
I wouldn't mandate that she not go

00:19:21.400 --> 00:19:23.250
but if she were my mother
I would tell her not to go.

00:19:23.250 --> 00:19:24.083
I mean so,

00:19:24.083 --> 00:19:25.150
we're not stupid.

00:19:25.150 --> 00:19:29.480
We should let people
make decisions on risk.

00:19:29.480 --> 00:19:32.750
- Yeah, so you mentioned knuckleheads

00:19:32.750 --> 00:19:35.120
and I'm here in California
as you may know,

00:19:35.120 --> 00:19:37.460
so I've got Gavin Newsom as my governor

00:19:37.460 --> 00:19:39.900
and I've got Eric Garcetti
as my mayor here in L.A.

00:19:39.900 --> 00:19:42.370
These are big governments progressives.

00:19:42.370 --> 00:19:45.690
So I'm gonna ask you for a
little life advice right now.

00:19:45.690 --> 00:19:46.523
For the first time

00:19:46.523 --> 00:19:47.660
since I moved to LA,

00:19:47.660 --> 00:19:49.860
I love it here, it's
85 and sunny every day,

00:19:49.860 --> 00:19:50.970
my life has thrived,

00:19:50.970 --> 00:19:52.810
I've got a great small business,

00:19:52.810 --> 00:19:54.630
I'm in my garage right now Senator,

00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:55.840
it's pretty sweet.

00:19:55.840 --> 00:19:57.780
But I am honestly thinking about leaving

00:19:57.780 --> 00:20:01.450
because I don't trust that these people

00:20:01.450 --> 00:20:03.200
will make the right decisions.

00:20:03.200 --> 00:20:04.560
And I wonder, just generally,

00:20:04.560 --> 00:20:07.120
what's your philosophy on,

00:20:07.120 --> 00:20:08.870
cause I think a lot of people
are seeing this right now.

00:20:08.870 --> 00:20:10.480
If they live in a state

00:20:10.480 --> 00:20:12.890
that their officials' ideas are

00:20:12.890 --> 00:20:15.380
totally incongruent with their beliefs,

00:20:15.380 --> 00:20:17.720
do you generally believe
in stay and fight,

00:20:17.720 --> 00:20:18.770
or would you say,

00:20:18.770 --> 00:20:21.260
no you can get on over to Kentucky,

00:20:21.260 --> 00:20:22.260
get on over to Florida,

00:20:22.260 --> 00:20:23.480
get on over to Texas,

00:20:23.480 --> 00:20:26.670
and go where maybe your
ideas are more in line?

00:20:26.670 --> 00:20:29.010
Cause I think this is like
the most unspoken thing

00:20:29.010 --> 00:20:30.083
